{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Problem\n\nvig runs in a repository, but the Projects page (#119) lists every project of the owner and needs a selection before a board appears. That is the wrong scope for a repo-rooted tool.\n\n## Spec\n\n- **Scope**: only projects linked to the current repository (`gh repo view --json projectsV2`). Drop the owner-wide `gh project list` as the default source.\n- **Default layout**: the board takes the full width; the `projects` list pane is **not placed** in the builtin layout.\n  - one linked project → its board is shown immediately on activation\n  - several → the header shows `Board: <title> (i/n)` and `p` / `P` cycle through them (or a popup like the branch selector)\n  - none → notice: \"No projects are linked to this repository (link one from the repository's Projects tab or `gh project link`)\"\n- **Keep the `projects` pane** as an optional pane: it stays implemented, and a user config that places it (`place \"projects\" …` in `page \"projects\" { layout { … } }`) gets the list back, driving the board via the existing `bind select=\"projects\" detail=\"board\"`. When placed it lists the same linked projects; an `a` toggle to show all owner projects is optional.\n- Loader: a `pane` block that is defined but not placed in `layout` must be allowed (inactive pane) — today every pane has to be placed exactly once. Only the placed panes participate in `tabs` cycling / focus; `bind` entries referring to an unplaced pane are ignored.\n- Board items: show every item of the project; cards whose content lives in another repository get a dimmed `owner/repo#n` prefix.\n- Detail (Fields), table mode and sorting stay as they are.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Linked-projects source + selection state (`p` / `P`, header label, empty notice)\n- [ ] Builtin `page \"projects\"` layout without the list pane; tabs `board` `detail`\n- [ ] Loader: allow unplaced panes (validation + tests); docs/config.md explains how to place `projects`\n- [ ] Cross-repository card prefix\n- [ ] README / README.ja / config.md; re-record `demo-projects` (board first)\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T11:02:14Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":128,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects view: scope to the repository's linked projects; board full width by default"}
